lantern-pr 1
# 11
#title LAN-117: add CodeQL workflow and private vulnerability reporting
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/11
#branch chore/codeql-security-policy
#base main
#opened 2026-11-09
#head 30cfcb949308b58ff451520472bfad958ac17cbd
#describe what Adds a CodeQL workflow for JavaScript and TypeScript and points the security policy at GitHub private vulnerability reporting.
#describe before Vulnerabilities were reported by e-mail only and no code scanning ran.
#describe after Reports go through the Security tab first, and CodeQL runs on pushes to main, pull requests and weekly.
#describe verified Typecheck, lint and the unit tests are green; the workflow YAML parses and its actions are SHA-pinned. The workflow itself is unrun.
+ .github/workflows/codeql.yml
~ SECURITY.md
#order .github/workflows/codeql.yml
#order SECURITY.md
#reason .github/workflows/codeql.yml Static analysis of the JavaScript and TypeScript code must run on every change and weekly to surface vulnerabilities.
#reason SECURITY.md Public repo needs a private reporting channel so vulnerabilities are not disclosed in public issues.
#story Reporting a vulnerability
#step actor A security researcher
#step action reports a problem in Lantern
#step subject the maintainers
#file SECURITY.md
#below interaction Uses the private GitHub advisory form, not a public issue
#below consequence Reports came by e-mail only => Reports arrive privately on GitHub
#story Code scanning
#step actor A contributor
#step action pushes or opens a pull request
#step subject the code scanner
#file .github/workflows/codeql.yml
#below interaction Sees security findings in the Security tab
#below consequence No automated security analysis => CodeQL scans every change and weekly
